cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI Character Index
message: >-
  If you use this project or its coverage data in academic work, please cite
  it using the metadata below. The index is a dataset that changes, so cite
  the publication you read: every build has an identifier and a date, and the
  site offers a ready-made citation carrying both. The specifications the
  index reads are third-party works and should be cited to their own
  publishers, not to this project.
type: dataset

# The authors of the index and of the data. Andrés Cotton and Matt Stults
# created the index and its method (the rubric, the scale, the prompt and the
# citation grammar, referenced below) and wrote most of the behaviour briefs.
# Polaris Collective maintains the project, runs the deployment and runs the
# judging: as of September 2026 the public publication carries runs of its
# own, so it is an author of the dataset. Each publication also computes its
# own credit from the runs and briefs it carries, and the site's citation of a
# build reads it from there.
authors:
  - given-names: Andrés
    family-names: Cotton
  - given-names: Matt
    family-names: Stults
  - name: Polaris Collective
    website: 'https://polariscollective.org'

contact:
  - name: Polaris Collective
    website: 'https://polariscollective.org'

abstract: >-
  A structured index of where published AI behaviour specifications
  address particular model behaviours. A panel of LLM judges reads each
  specification whole, marks the passages that bear on each behaviour and
  gives the document a 0 to 4 depth, and every citation is recorded with a
  locator resolving to verbatim spec text.

# This fork, which is what the URL below serves. The original stands alone and
# is the one to clone: https://github.com/AndresCotton/ai-character-index
repository-code: 'https://github.com/polariscollective/ai-character-index'
url: 'https://ai-character-index.vercel.app/spec-reader/'
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-08-24'
keywords:
  - AI alignment
  - model specifications
  - behaviour coverage
  - LLM evaluation

# The method, credited on its own line: it is the same whoever runs it.
references:
  - type: software
    title: AI Character Index
    abstract: >-
      The original, standalone AI Character Index, and the method this index
      runs: the depth rubric and its scale, the judging prompt and the
      citation grammar.
    authors:
      - given-names: Andrés
        family-names: Cotton
      - given-names: Matt
        family-names: Stults
    repository-code: 'https://github.com/AndresCotton/ai-character-index'
    url: 'https://ai-character-index.pages.dev'
